#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:6
msgid "Security reports"
msgstr "安全报告"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:8
msgid ""
"Security is extremely important to us at Read the Docs. We follow generally "
"accepted industry standards to protect the personal information submitted to"
" us, both during transmission and once we receive it. In the spirit of "
"transparency, we are committed to responsible reporting and disclosure of "
"security issues."
msgstr ""
"安全对 Read the Docs "
"至关重要。我们遵循业界公认的标准保护提交给我们的个人信息，无论是在传输过程中还是接收之后。秉持透明精神，我们致力于负责任地报告和披露安全问题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:17
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "目录"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:21
msgid ":doc:`/legal/security-policy`"
msgstr ":doc:`/legal/security-policy`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:22
msgid ""
"Read our policy for security, which we base our security handling and "
"reporting on."
msgstr "阅读我们的安全政策，我们的安全处理和报告均以此为依据。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:25
msgid "Supported versions"
msgstr "受支持的版本"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:27
msgid ""
"Only the latest version of Read the Docs will receive security updates. We "
"don't support security updates for :doc:`custom installations </open-source-"
"philosophy>` of Read the Docs."
msgstr ""
"只有 Read the Docs 的最新版本会收到安全更新。我们不为 Read the Docs 的 :doc:`定制安装 </open-source-"
"philosophy>` 提供安全更新。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:31
msgid "Reporting a security issue"
msgstr "报告安全问题"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:33
msgid ""
"If you believe you've discovered a security issue at Read the Docs, please "
"contact us at **security@readthedocs.org** (optionally using our "
":ref:`security:PGP key`). We request that you please not publicly disclose "
"the issue until it has been addressed by us."
msgstr ""
"若你发现 Read the Docs 存在安全问题，请联系 **security@readthedocs.org** （可选用我们的 "
":ref:`security:PGP key` ）。我们请求你在我们处理完毕前不要公开披露该问题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:37
msgid "You can expect:"
msgstr "你可以期待："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:39
msgid "We will respond acknowledging your email typically within one business day."
msgstr "我们通常会在一个工作日内回复确认你的邮件。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:40
msgid ""
"We will follow up if and when we have confirmed the issue with a timetable "
"for the fix."
msgstr "确认问题后，我们会跟进并给出修复时间表。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:41
msgid "We will notify you when the issue is fixed."
msgstr "问题修复后我们会通知你。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:42
msgid ""
"We will create a `GitHub advisory`_ and publish it when the issue has been "
"fixed and deployed in our platforms."
msgstr "问题修复并部署到我们平台后，我们会创建 `GitHub advisory`_ 并发布。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:48
msgid "PGP key"
msgstr "PGP 密钥"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:50
msgid ""
"You may use this :download:`PGP key </_static/security/pgpkey.txt>` to "
"securely communicate with us and to verify signed messages you receive from "
"us."
msgstr "你可以使用此 :download:`PGP 密钥 </_static/security/pgpkey.txt>` 与我们安全通信，并验证你收到的签名消息。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:54
msgid "Bug bounties"
msgstr "漏洞赏金"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:56
msgid ""
"While we sincerely appreciate and encourage reports of suspected security "
"problems, please note that the Read the Docs is an open source project, and "
"**does not run any bug bounty programs**. But we will gladly give credit to "
"you and/or your organization for responsibly reporting security issues."
msgstr ""
"我们真诚感谢并鼓励报告疑似安全问题，但请注意 Read the Docs 是开源项目，**不运行任何漏洞赏金计划** "
"。不过，对负责任地报告安全问题的你和/或你的组织，我们乐于给予致谢。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:61
msgid "Security issue archive"
msgstr "安全问题归档"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:63
msgid ""
"You can see all past reports at "
"https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/security/advisories."
msgstr ""
"你可以在 https://github.com/readthedocs/readthedocs.org/security/advisories "
"查看所有过往报告。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:66
msgid "Version 3.2.0"
msgstr "Version 3.2.0"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:68
msgid ""
":ref:`changelog:Version 3.2.0` resolved an issue where a specially crafted "
"request could result in a DNS query to an arbitrary domain."
msgstr ":ref:`changelog:Version 3.2.0` 修复了一个问题：特制请求可能导致对任意域名的 DNS 查询。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:71
msgid ""
"This issue was found by `Cyber Smart Defence "
"<https://www.cybersmartdefence.com/>`_ who reported it as part of a security"
" audit to a firm running a local installation of Read the Docs."
msgstr ""
"该问题由 `Cyber Smart Defence <https://www.cybersmartdefence.com/>`_ 发现，他们在为某家运行"
" Read the Docs 本地安装的公司做安全审计时报告了此问题。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:77
msgid "Release 2.3.0"
msgstr "Release 2.3.0"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:79
msgid ""
":ref:`changelog:Version 2.3.0` resolves a security issue with translations "
"on our community hosting site that allowed users to modify the hosted path "
"of a target project by adding it as a translation project of their own "
"project. A check was added to ensure project ownership before adding the "
"project as a translation."
msgstr ""
":ref:`changelog:Version 2.3.0` "
"修复了社区托管站点上翻译功能的一个安全问题：用户可将目标项目添加为自有项目的翻译项目，从而修改其托管路径。现已增加检查，在添加为翻译项目前确认项目所有权。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/security.rst:84
msgid ""
"In order to add a project as a translation now, users must now first be "
"granted ownership in the translation project."
msgstr "如今要将项目添加为翻译，用户必须先获得该翻译项目的所有权。"

